<% content_for :title, "On Impulsivity | Bipolar Sober" %>

<style>
  .impulsivity-page {
    background: #080808;
    color: #fff;
    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
  }

  .impulsivity-page *,
  .impulsivity-page *::before,
  .impulsivity-page *::after {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .impulsivity-hero {
    min-height: 85vh;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 80px 6%;
    background-color: #080808;
    background-image:
      linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(8, 8, 8, .55), transparent),
      url("<%= asset_path('bipolar_impulsivity_desktop.png') %>");
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center;
  }

  .impulsivity-hero-content {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .impulsivity-eyebrow {
    max-width: 440px;
    margin: 0 0 28px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.6;
    letter-spacing: .12em;
  }

  .impulsivity-hero h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(44px, 7vw, 106px);
    font-weight: 900;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: .95;
    letter-spacing: -.055em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .impulsivity-hero h1 span {
    display: block;
  }

  .impulsivity-intro {
    margin: 32px 0 0;
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1.6vw, 22px);
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .impulsivity-quote {
    padding: 48px 6%;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .impulsivity-quote blockquote {
    max-width: 1000px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .impulsivity-quote blockquote p {
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    color: #eaff00;
    font-size: clamp(24px, 3.5vw, 46px);
    font-weight: 900;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .impulsivity-quote cite {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-style: normal;
  }

  .impulsivity-section {
    padding: 72px 6%;
  }

  .impulsivity-section-inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .85fr) minmax(0, 1.15fr);
    gap: 60px;
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .impulsivity-number {
    margin: 0 0 22px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: .12em;
  }

  .impulsivity-section h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(36px, 4.5vw, 68px);
    font-weight: 900;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: .95;
    letter-spacing: -.045em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .impulsivity-copy {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .impulsivity-copy p {
    margin: 0 0 22px;
  }

  .impulsivity-copy p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .impulsivity-copy ul {
    margin: 0 0 24px;
    padding-left: 22px;
  }

  .impulsivity-copy li {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .impulsivity-pink {
    background: #ff1493;
    color: #080808;
  }

  .impulsivity-yellow {
    background: #eaff00;
    color: #080808;
  }

  .impulsivity-purple {
    background: #8a00ff;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .impulsivity-black {
    background: #080808;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .impulsivity-white {
    background: #fff;
    color: #080808;
  }

  .impulsivity-takeaway {
    padding-top: 22px;
    border-top: 3px solid currentColor;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .impulsivity-footer {
    padding: 40px 6%;
    border-top: 1px solid #444;
  }

  .impulsivity-footer-inner {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 24px;
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .impulsivity-footer a {
    color: #eaff00;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.5;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .impulsivity-footer a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .impulsivity-footer a:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid #ff1493;
    outline-offset: 6px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .impulsivity-hero {
      min-height: 88svh;
      align-items: flex-start;
      padding: 48px 6% 60px;
      background-image:
        url("<%= asset_path('bipolar_impulsivity_mobile.png') %>");
      background-position: center bottom;
    }

    .impulsivity-eyebrow {
      margin-bottom: 24px;
      font-size: 10px;
    }

    .impulsivity-hero h1 {
      font-size: clamp(32px, 10.5vw, 80px);
    }

    .impulsivity-intro {
      margin-top: 24px;
      font-size: 14px;
    }

    .impulsivity-section {
      padding: 48px 6%;
    }

    .impulsivity-section-inner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 28px;
    }

    .impulsivity-section h2 {
      font-size: clamp(36px, 10vw, 58px);
    }

    .impulsivity-copy {
      font-size: 16px;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .impulsivity-number {
      margin-bottom: 16px;
    }
  }
</style>

<main class="impulsivity-page">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="impulsivity-hero" aria-labelledby="impulsivity-title">
    <div class="impulsivity-hero-content">

      <p class="impulsivity-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / BIPOLAR / IMPULSIVITY
      </p>

      <h1 id="impulsivity-title">
        <span>ON</span>
        <span>IMPULSIVITY.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="impulsivity-intro">
        THE URGE. THE EXCUSE.<br>
        THE FUCK-IT MOMENT.<br>
        THE SPACE BEFORE YOU ACT.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- QUOTE -->
  <section class="impulsivity-quote" aria-label="Opening quote">
    <blockquote>
      <p>
        “Your scientists were so preoccupied with whether or not
        they could, they didn’t stop to think if they should.”
      </p>
      <cite>— Ian Malcolm</cite>
    </blockquote>
  </section>


  <!-- 01 / THE URGE -->
  <section class="impulsivity-section impulsivity-pink">
    <div class="impulsivity-section-inner">

      <div class="impulsivity-section-heading">
        <p class="impulsivity-number">01 / THE FUCK-IT MOMENT</p>

        <h2>
          TWO WORDS.<br>
          EXPENSIVE<br>
          AS FUCK.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="impulsivity-copy">
        <p>
          Fuck it. Sometimes the cost is money. Sometimes it is
          sobriety, safety, or the stability you have worked to build.
          You want the thing, the experience, the relief.
          The consequences feel like another version of you’s problem.
        </p>

        <p>
          Overspending and substance use can both involve reaching
          for an immediate change in how you feel. Alcoholism is
          more complex than impulsivity, and cravings can involve
          planning. Notice the sudden decision and the hours spent
          negotiating yourself into permission.
        </p>

        <p class="impulsivity-takeaway">
          The urge deserves attention before it becomes a decision
          with consequences.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 02 / PERMISSION -->
  <section class="impulsivity-section impulsivity-yellow">
    <div class="impulsivity-section-inner">

      <div class="impulsivity-section-heading">
        <p class="impulsivity-number">02 / CHECK THE ARGUMENT</p>

        <h2>
          SOUNDS<br>
          REASONABLE.<br>
          LOOK<br>
          AGAIN.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="impulsivity-copy">
        <p>
          “I deserve it.” “I’ll figure out the money.”
          “One won’t hurt.” “Today was unbearable.”
          Ask whether the explanation considers your whole situation
          or clears a path toward what you already want.
        </p>

        <p>
          Wanting relief is understandable. It does not establish
          that alcohol, weed, or another purchase will meet the need
          without adding problems. Consider the promise alongside
          your own history.
        </p>

        <p>
          “I already messed up, so whatever” can turn one harmful
          decision into several. You can interrupt the sequence
          after it starts. The next choice still matters.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 03 / THE NEED -->
  <section class="impulsivity-section impulsivity-purple">
    <div class="impulsivity-section-inner">

      <div class="impulsivity-section-heading">
        <p class="impulsivity-number">03 / UNDERNEATH THE URGE</p>

        <h2>
          WHAT ARE<br>
          YOU TRYING<br>
          TO CHANGE?
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="impulsivity-copy">
        <p>
          What do you want the substance, purchase, or sudden action
          to provide? Relief from pain? Quiet? Excitement?
          Escape from boredom, anger, or depression?
          Understanding the need gives you something specific to address.
        </p>

        <p>
          A part of you may be exhausted by budgeting, symptoms,
          appointments, and consequences. Listen to what it needs
          while giving the part that wants sobriety and stability
          a voice too.
        </p>

        <p>
          Bring ordinary things you are protecting into the decision:
          money for a bill, waking without a hangover, being available
          for something you care about. Let the future enter
          the conversation.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 04 / THE PAUSE -->
  <section class="impulsivity-section impulsivity-black">
    <div class="impulsivity-section-inner">

      <div class="impulsivity-section-heading">
        <p class="impulsivity-number">04 / CREATE SOME ROOM</p>

        <h2>
          WANTING.<br>
          PAUSING.<br>
          CHOOSING.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="impulsivity-copy">
        <p>
          Notice the demand that discomfort end right fucking now.
          Give yourself a short stretch of time to postpone acting
          and bring support closer. You do not have to enjoy
          the feeling to take a protective step.
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>Close the shopping app or leave the purchase unfinished.</li>
          <li>Step away from access to alcohol or other substances.</li>
          <li>Say, “I want to drink, and I’m starting to justify it.”</li>
          <li>Ask someone to stay on the phone or help you follow your relapse plan.</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="impulsivity-takeaway">
          A craving can be present without becoming a command.
          Let your surroundings and support plan help hold the gap.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 05 / SAFEGUARDS -->
  <section class="impulsivity-section impulsivity-white">
    <div class="impulsivity-section-inner">

      <div class="impulsivity-section-heading">
        <p class="impulsivity-number">05 / HELP YOUR FUTURE SELF</p>

        <h2>
          MAKE THE<br>
          PAUSE<br>
          EASIER.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="impulsivity-copy">
        <p>
          Build safeguards while you have room to choose them.
          Remove saved payment details, turn off sales notifications,
          and set a waiting period for purchases. Keep recovery
          contacts accessible and decide what to do when using
          starts becoming a plan.
        </p>

        <p>
          Respond to the need too. Eat if you are hungry.
          Reach out if you need connection. Use your established
          pain plan and tell your care team when it is insufficient.
          Make the evening smaller when everything feels overwhelming.
        </p>

        <p>
          Treat the pause as a challenge in resourcefulness:
          given these circumstances, what protective action is
          available? Success can mean getting through this stretch
          without adding another problem.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 06 / ACCOUNTABILITY -->
  <section class="impulsivity-section impulsivity-yellow">
    <div class="impulsivity-section-inner">

      <div class="impulsivity-section-heading">
        <p class="impulsivity-number">06 / THE NEXT CHOICE</p>

        <h2>
          REPAIR.<br>
          RECONNECT.<br>
          KEEP GOING.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="impulsivity-copy">
        <p>
          Bipolar disorder, ADHD, and alcohol use disorder belong
          in your understanding of your patterns. Taking your
          medication does not mean you will never need more support.
          Speak up when urges intensify or safeguards stop feeling
          sufficient.
        </p>

        <p>
          If you acted, address what needs care now. Cancel or return
          the purchase where possible. Review the money. If you used,
          tell someone who can help you respond and reconnect with
          treatment. You can ask before shame passes.
        </p>

        <p>
          What came before the urge? What made acting seem acceptable?
          Where could support enter earlier? These questions give you
          something to change beyond calling yourself a fucking idiot.
        </p>

        <p class="impulsivity-takeaway">
          You can want relief and remain committed to recovery.
          Your future needs care when the present feels urgent.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- NAVIGATION -->
  <nav class="impulsivity-footer" aria-label="Bipolar topic navigation">
    <div class="impulsivity-footer-inner">
      <%= link_to "← BACK TO BIPOLAR", bipolar_path %>
      <%= link_to "EXPLORE PERSPECTIVES →", bipolar_perspectives_path %>
    </div>
  </nav>

</main>